#: theory.md:1
msgid "AlphaFold-Metainference"
msgstr "AlphaFold-Metainference"

#: theory.md:2
msgid "Context"
msgstr "背景"

#: theory.md:4
msgid ""
"The application of deep learning methods to the protein folding problem has "
"transformed our ability to generate accurate models of the native states of "
"proteins from the knowledge of their amino acid sequences. The initial "
"predictions of the native structures of proteins have also been recently "
"extended to protein complexes. These advances have prompted the question of "
"whether it is possible to use this type of approach for the prediction of "
"the conformational fluctuations of the native states of folded proteins, and"
" more generally for the characterisation of the structural properties of the"
" native states of disordered proteins. Support for this idea comes from the "
"observation that AlphaFold performs as well as current state-of-the-art "
"predictors of protein disorder. It has also been reported that the predicted"
" aligned error (PAE) maps from AlphaFold are correlated with the distance "
"variation matrices from molecular dynamics simulations, suggesting that "
"AlphaFold provides information about the dynamics of proteins in addition to"
" their structures."
msgstr ""
"Protein Folding 問題への Deep Learning の適用により、アミノ酸配列から Native State "
"の正確なモデルを作る能力が大きく進歩しました。単独タンパク質の構造予測は、最近では複合体にも拡張されています。この進歩により、Folded "
"Protein の Native State の Conformational Fluctuation や、より一般に Disordered "
"Protein の Native State の構造特性も予測できるのではないか、という問いが生まれました。AlphaFold が最新の "
"Disorder 予測器と同程度に機能するという観測も、この考えを支持します。また AlphaFold の Predicted Aligned "
"Error (PAE) Map が MD の距離変動 Matrix と相関すると報告され、構造だけでなく Dynamics "
"の情報も含むことが示唆されています。"

#: theory.md:6
msgid ""
"Since the native states of disordered proteins can be represented in terms "
"of ensembles of conformations with statistical weights obeying the Boltzmann"
" distribution, a relevant goal is to extend AlphaFold to predict structural "
"ensembles of partially disordered proteins. In this work, we propose an "
"approach to perform this task by basing this approach on the observation "
"that AlphaFold can predict inter-residue distances even for disordered "
"proteins, despite having been trained on folded proteins and combining such "
"information with molecular dynamics within the Metainference framework."
msgstr ""
"Disordered Protein の Native State は、Boltzmann 分布に従う統計的重みを持つ Conformation の "
"Ensemble で表せます。そのため AlphaFold を拡張し、部分的に Disordered なタンパク質の Structural "
"Ensemble を予測することは重要です。本研究では、Folded Protein で学習した AlphaFold が Disordered "
"Protein の残基間距離も予測できるという観測を基に、その情報と MD を Metainference で統合する方法を提案します。"

#: theory.md:9
msgid "Theory"
msgstr "理論"

#: theory.md:11
msgid ""
"More information about AlphaFold-Metainference can be found "
"[here](https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.11.09.622758v1)"
msgstr ""
"AlphaFold-Metainference の詳細は "
"[こちら](https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.11.09.622758v1) にあります。"

#: theory.md:13
msgid ""
"***AlphaFold distance map prediction.*** Average inter-residue distances of "
"disordered proteins can be predicted through the distogram head of AlphaFold"
" using this colab "
"[notebook](https://github.com/zshengyu14/ColabFold_distmats/blob/main/AlphaFold2.ipynb)."
" These distances are defined as those between the β carbon atom positions "
"for all amino acids except glycine, for which the α carbon atom positions "
"are instead employed. The multiple sequence alignment (MSA) is conducted by "
"MMseqs2 (default setting) on BFD/MGnify and Uniclust30. Model 1.1.1 of "
"AlphaFold (default setting) is used for the predictions, with no structural "
"templates. AlphaFold describes the distribution of inter-residue distances "
"into 64 bins of equal width, covering the range from 2.15625 to 21.84375 Å, "
"with the last bin also including distances longer than 21.84375 Å. For each "
"pair of residues ($i$ and $j$), AlphaFold predicts the probability "
"$p_{ij}^{b}$ that their distance is within bin $b$. The predicted distance "
"${\\widehat{d}}_{ij}$ of the predicted distribution of the distances between"
" residue $i$ and $j$ are esimated as"
msgstr ""
"***AlphaFold の Distance Map 予測。*** Disordered Protein の平均残基間距離は、AlphaFold の "
"Distogram Head と、この Colab "
"[Notebook](https://github.com/zshengyu14/ColabFold_distmats/blob/main/AlphaFold2.ipynb)"
" で予測できます。Glycine 以外は β Carbon、Glycine は α Carbon 間の距離です。Multiple Sequence "
"Alignment (MSA) は MMseqs2 の既定設定で BFD/MGnify と Uniclust30 に対して行います。構造 "
"Template を使わず、既定の AlphaFold Model 1.1.1 で予測します。残基間距離は2.15625〜21.84375 Å "
"の等幅64 Bin で表し、最後の Bin は21.84375 Å より長い距離も含みます。各残基対（$i$、$j$）について、距離が Bin $b$ "
"に入る確率 $p_{ij}^{b}$ を予測します。残基 $i$、$j$ の距離予測分布からの予測距離 ${\\widehat{d}}_{ij}$ "
"は次のように推定します。"

# Literal notation or identifier intentionally preserved.
#: theory.md:31
msgid "$\\hat{d_{ij}}=\\sum_{b=1}^{64} d^{b} p_{ij}^{b} $"
msgstr "$\\hat{d_{ij}}=\\sum_{b=1}^{64} d^{b} p_{ij}^{b} $"

#: theory.md:34
msgid "where $d^{b}$ represents the central value of bin $b$."
msgstr "$d^{b}$ は Bin $b$ の中心値です。"

#: theory.md:36
msgid ""
"***Metainference*.** [Metainference](https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.1501177)"
" is a Bayesian inference method that enables the determination of structural"
" ensembles by combining prior information and experimental data according to"
" the maximum entropy principle. In AF-MI, Metainference is implemented by "
"using the distance matrix $\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$ predicted by AlphaFold as "
"pseudo-experimental data. By design, metainference can disentangle "
"structural heterogeneity from systematic errors, such as force field or "
"forward model inaccuracies, random errors in the data, and errors due to the"
" limited sample size of the ensemble. The molecular simulations are carried "
"out according to the metainference energy function, $E = - "
"k_{B}T\\log\\left( p_{MI} \\right)$, where $k_{B}$ is the Boltzmann "
"constant, *T* is the temperature, and $p_{MI}$ is the metainference, "
"maximum-entropy-compatible, posterior probability"
msgstr ""
"***Metainference。*** [Metainference](https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.1501177)"
" は、Maximum Entropy 原理に従って事前情報と実験データを統合し、Structural Ensemble を決める Bayesian "
"Inference 法です。AF-MI では、AlphaFold の距離 Matrix $\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$ "
"を擬似実験データとして用います。構造の不均一性を、Force Field・Forward Model の不正確さなどの系統誤差、データの Random "
"Error、有限 Sample 数による誤差から分離できます。シミュレーションは Metainference のエネルギー関数 $E = - "
"k_{B}T\\log\\left( p_{MI} \\right)$ に従います。$k_{B}$ は Boltzmann 定数、*T* "
"は温度、$p_{MI}$ は Maximum Entropy と整合する Metainference の事後確率です。"

# Mathematical expression and equation number intentionally preserved.
#: theory.md:50
msgid ""
"$p_{MI}\\left( \\mathbf{X},\\sigma^{SEM},\\sigma^{B} \\right|\\mathbf{D}) = "
"\\ \\prod_{r = 1}^{N_{R}}{p\\ \\left( X_{r} \\right)\\prod_{i = "
"1}^{N_{D}}{p(\\mathbf{D|\\ "
"X},\\sigma_{i}^{SEM},\\sigma_{r,i}^{Β})p(\\sigma_{r,i})\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ "
"\\ \\ \\ }}$ (3)"
msgstr ""
"$p_{MI}\\left( \\mathbf{X},\\sigma^{SEM},\\sigma^{B} \\right|\\mathbf{D}) = "
"\\ \\prod_{r = 1}^{N_{R}}{p\\ \\left( X_{r} \\right)\\prod_{i = "
"1}^{N_{D}}{p(\\mathbf{D|\\ "
"X},\\sigma_{i}^{SEM},\\sigma_{r,i}^{Β})p(\\sigma_{r,i})\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ "
"\\ \\ \\ }}$ (3)"

#: theory.md:53
msgid ""
"In this formula, **X** denotes the vector comprising the atomic coordinates "
"of the structural ensemble, consisting of individual replicas $X_r$ ($N_R$ "
"in total), $σ^{SEM}$ the error associated to the limited number of replicas "
"in the ensemble, $σ_B$ the random and systematic errors in the prior "
"molecular dynamics forcefield as well as in the forward model and the data, "
"and $\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$ the AF distance matrix. Note that $σ^{SEM}$ is "
"calculated for each data point ($σ_i^{SEM}$), while $σ^B$ is computed for "
"each data point *i* and replica *r* as $σ_{r,i}^B$. The functional form of "
"the likelihood $p(\\mathbf{d}^{AF}\\|\\mathbf{X}, σ_i^{SEM} , σ_{r,i}^B)$ is"
" a Gaussian function"
msgstr ""
"**X** は Structural Ensemble の原子座標の Vector で、計 $N_R$ 個の Replica $X_r$ "
"からなります。$σ^{SEM}$ は有限 Replica 数の誤差、$σ_B$ は事前の MD Force Field・Forward "
"Model・データの Random Error と系統誤差、$\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$ は AF Distance Matrix "
"です。$σ^{SEM}$ はデータ点ごとに $σ_i^{SEM}$ として計算し、$σ^B$ は各データ点 *i*・Replica *r* ごとに "
"$σ_{r,i}^B$ として求めます。尤度 $p(\\mathbf{d}^{AF}\\|\\mathbf{X}, σ_i^{SEM} , "
"σ_{r,i}^B)$ は Gaussian 関数です。"

#: theory.md:67
msgid ""
"where $d_{i,j}(X)$ represents the forward model for data point *i,j,* namely"
" the *i,j* distance calculated in the ensemble. For multiple replicas, the "
"metainference energy function is"
msgstr ""
"$d_{i,j}(X)$ はデータ点 *i,j* の Forward Model、すなわち Ensemble で計算する *i,j* 間距離です。複数 "
"Replica の Metainference エネルギー関数は次のようになります。"

#: theory.md:73
msgid "where $E_σ$ corresponds to the energy term associated with the errors"
msgstr "$E_σ$ は誤差に対応するエネルギー項です。"

#: theory.md:77
msgid ""
"Finally, $E_{MD}$ corresponds to the potential energy function of the "
"molecular dynamics force field, which in this case is the CALVADOS 2 force "
"field. While the space of conformations $X_r$ is sampled through multi-"
"replica simulations (in this tutorial we used six replicas, however the "
"larger this number the better) the error parameters for each datapoint "
"$σ_{r,i}^B$ are sampled through a Gibbs sampling scheme at each time step. "
"The range of the error sampling in this tutorial is set to\\[0.0001,10\\] "
"and the associated trial move error perturbation of the Gibbs sampling is "
"set 0.1. For more information on how to select these parameters, refer "
"[here](https://link.springer.com/protocol/10.1007/978-1-4939-9608-7_13). The"
" error parameter due to the limited number of replicas used to estimate the "
"forward model ($σ^{SEM}$) is calculated on the fly by window averaging every"
" 200 steps of molecular dynamics."
msgstr ""
"$E_{MD}$ は MD Force Field の Potential Energy 関数で、ここでは CALVADOS 2 "
"です。Conformation $X_r$ は Multi-replica で Sampling します。この Tutorial は6 Replica "
"ですが、多いほどよいでしょう。各データ点の誤差パラメータ $σ_{r,i}^B$ は各 Time Step で Gibbs Sampling "
"します。ここでの範囲は \\[0.0001,10\\]、Gibbs Sampling の Trial Move の誤差摂動は0.1です。選び方の詳細は "
"[こちら](https://link.springer.com/protocol/10.1007/978-1-4939-9608-7_13) "
"を参照してください。Forward Model の推定に使う Replica 数が有限であることによる誤差 ($σ^{SEM}$) は、MD の200 "
"Step ごとの Window Average で On-the-fly に計算します。"

#: theory.md:90
msgid "**AF-MI advantages**"
msgstr "**AF-MI の利点**"

#: theory.md:92
msgid ""
"By combining AlphaFold inter-resiude distance data with the CALVADOS 2 "
"forcefield to retrieve structural ensembles of proteins are:"
msgstr ""
"AlphaFold の残基間距離と CALVADOS 2 Force Field を組み合わせて Structural Ensemble "
"を得る利点は、次のとおりです。"

#: theory.md:93
msgid ""
"The high convergence speed due to the coarse grained model and a "
"metadynamics bias"
msgstr "Coarse-grained Model と Metadynamics Bias による速い収束。"

#: theory.md:94
msgid ""
"The increased accuracy in modeling partially ordered protein interactions "
"relyig on the introduction of AlphaFold-based distance restraints"
msgstr ""
"AlphaFold に基づく Distance Restraint の導入による、部分的に Ordered なタンパク質の相互作用モデルの精度向上。"

#: theory.md:118
msgid ""
"Using as benchmarking comparison a subset of 6 proteins from Tesei et. al. "
"Nature 2024 where we have available experimental Rg data and CALVADOS 2 has "
"larger deviations from experimental Rg, we provide with a systematic manner "
"of selecting AF distances as restraints in Fig. SX.4. This approach shows "
"than when a protein has a Kyte-doolittle hydropathy of less than -1.4, "
"signifying hydrophilic character and at least a 5 residue stretch with "
"plddt\\>75, then selecting AF distances with PAE\\<10 has better agreement "
"with experimental Rgs (see NLS, Msh6-NRT). Otherwise a PAE\\<5 is used (see "
"AN16,CTCF-RD,Eralpha-NTD,CortactinCRH). CALVADOS 2 is trained based on "
"residue hydrophobicity and alphafold suffers in predicting structures of low"
" plddt regions that are equipped with flexible residues. The motivation for "
"the combined hydropathy and plddt criterion stems from the fact that if any "
"corrections need to be applied either to calvados or to alphafold so that "
"they generate better ensembles, these will be where a hydrophobicity-based "
"model alone faces challenges in predicting interactions. In Fig. SX4 we show"
" that CALVADOS 2 can be assisted by AF-MI in generating ensembles that "
"better agree with Rg data."
msgstr ""
"実験 Rg が得られ、CALVADOS 2 の実験値からのずれが大きい、Tesei らの Nature 2024 の6タンパク質を比較対象に、AF "
"距離を Restraint として選ぶ体系的な方法を図 SX.4 に示します。Kyte-Doolittle Hydropathy "
"が-1.4未満で親水的であり、plddt\\>75 が5残基以上続く場合、PAE\\<10 の距離を選ぶと実験 Rg "
"とよく一致します（NLS、Msh6-NRT）。それ以外は PAE\\<5 を使います（AN16、CTCF-RD、Eralpha-"
"NTD、CortactinCRH）。CALVADOS 2 は残基の Hydrophobicity に基づき学習され、AlphaFold "
"は柔軟な残基を含む低 plddt 領域の構造予測を苦手とします。Hydropathy と plddt を組み合わせる理由は、Ensemble "
"を改善するため CALVADOS や AlphaFold を補正すべき場所は、Hydrophobicity "
"のみのモデルで相互作用予測が難しい場所だと考えられるためです。図 SX4 は、AF-MI によって CALVADOS 2 が Rg により一致する "
"Ensemble を生成できることを示します。"

#: theory.md:137
msgid ""
"Therefore, we use as restraints a subset of the full "
"$\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$matrix by considering distances between amino acids at "
"least 3 residues apart, and with a Predicted Alignment Error (PAE) under 5 Å"
" or 10 Å according to the abovementioned distance selection rule and "
"excluding $p_{i,j}(r \\geq 21.84\\ Å\\ ) > 0.02$. Also, based on the fact "
"that C2 coarse grained model used in the AF-MI simulations does maintain "
"secondary structure, we employed the predicted local distance difference "
"test (pLDDT) score in AlphaFold to select the inter-residue distances "
"predicted with higher confidence and hence predicted to correspond to "
"structured regions. Sequence regions of at least two residues with a pLDDT "
"score \\>0.75 were hence considered structured regions and were restrained "
"to the AlphaFold-predicted structure by using an upper root mean square "
"distance (RMSD) wall. The residue distances corresponding to these "
"structured regions where excluded from the distance restraints set. This "
"action may not be necessary if one uses all-atom force fields that are able "
"to maintain the protein secondary structure. The PLUMED input files for AF-"
"MI can be found in (<https://zenodo.org/record/7756138>). The code to "
"prepare an AF-MI simulation can be found in (Github "
"<https://github.com/vendruscolo-lab/AlphaFold-IDP>)"
msgstr ""
"したがって、完全な $\\mathbf{d}^{AF}$ Matrix の一部を Restraint に使います。3残基以上離れ、上記の規則による "
"Predicted Alignment Error (PAE) が5 Å または10 Å 未満で、$p_{i,j}(r \\geq 21.84\\ "
"Å\\ ) > 0.02$ を除外した距離を選びます。また、AF-MI の C2 Coarse-grained Model が Secondary "
"Structure を維持することに基づき、AlphaFold の Predicted Local Distance Difference Test "
"(pLDDT) で、高信頼度かつ Structured 領域に対応すると予測される距離を選びます。pLDDT \\>0.75 の2残基以上の領域を "
"Structured とみなし、RMSD Upper Wall で AF 予測構造に拘束します。その領域内の残基間距離は Distance "
"Restraint から除外します。Secondary Structure を維持できる All-atom Force Field "
"なら、この処理は不要な場合があります。AF-MI の PLUMED 入力は "
"(<https://zenodo.org/record/7756138>)、準備用コードは (GitHub "
"<https://github.com/vendruscolo-lab/AlphaFold-IDP>) にあります。"

